WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.630
Viruses. From influenza to the common cold,
we’ve all had experiences with these nasty

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.049
diseases. They’re easy to catch, quickly
transferring from one host to another through

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:18.040
proximity or physical contact. This also means
that viruses are easily spread, and if the

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.320
number of infected grows beyond what’s treatable,
it can cripple the entire world’s health

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.840
infrastructure.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.930
Overrun hospitals, behavioral mandates, and
constant death are all elements of a worldwide

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:36.239
pandemic. It’s no wonder why zombie outbreaks
and lab-grown diseases are such common premises

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:41.800
for horror movies and video games. Diseases
are downright scary, and it’s most likely

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.370
because the world has been overtaken by disease
on multiple occasions that makes them so frightening.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:54.430
The bubonic plague, the great influenza pandemic,
and even the COVID-19 pandemic are all events

00:00:54.430 --> 00:01:00.230
that have wiped out significant portions of
humanity, and if left unchecked, a viral disease

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:03.559
might be able to wipe out every last one of
us.

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:08.610
Sure, you can take measures to keep yourself
safe, but who’s to say a mutation isn’t

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:14.060
out of the question? A disease altering its
own biology to overcome resistance and continue

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.890
its spread could be a germaphobe’s nightmare,
and have serious consequences for the entire

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.040
world. Of course, we’re still talking about
ordinary diseases, but what about when the

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:30.720
virus is anything but normal? What if it falls
under that umbrella that could be termed…

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.840
anomalous. Enter the SCP Foundation. For them,
anomalous viruses are some of the hardest

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.890
to secure, contain, and protect the world
from.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.490
It’s not hard to imagine why, either. Containing
viruses often involves the spread of safety

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:51.750
precautions and information, sometimes distributions
of vaccinations and medicine. Basically, to

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.210
stop a virus, people need to first know what
they’re dealing with. When you’re operating

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.470
under the veil of secrecy that the Foundation
has to maintain, your options for information

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.390
dispersal become a lot more complicated. Of
course, by nature of being anomalous, the

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.800
diseases the Foundation has to deal with are
a lot stranger, and definitely more dangerous

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.380
than just another strain of the flu.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:20.690
Perhaps you’re already familiar with SCP-008,
the infectious disease codenamed the “zombie

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.980
plague”, that shuts down a victim’s body
and decays it heavily, but the SCP Foundation’s

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:33.930
Russian database has a deadly virus of its
own. SCP-1007-RU, is also known as the Nietzsche

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:39.390
Virus. It’s nicknamed after the famous German
philosopher, who coined the term ‘God is

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.640
Dead’ and explored themes of nihilism, an
ideology that delves into the meaninglessness

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:51.210
of life, the universe, and humanity’s existence.
If that doesn’t clue you in that this anomaly

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:56.250
is horrifying, then just wait until we dive
into the file itself.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:02.940
SCP-1007-RU is, given it’s viral and infectious
nature, kept in a high security containment

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.411
chamber intended to seal the anomaly away
from the world. The chamber is outfitted with

00:03:07.411 --> 00:03:16.090
a triple-airlock system that prevents accidental
leakage and unwanted access. Entry into SCP-1007-RU’s

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.681
containment chamber comes with its own set
of Special Containment Procedures. Researchers

00:03:20.681 --> 00:03:26.040
must outfit themselves in an insulated, protective
suit that allows no material from inside the

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:32.590
chamber to make contact with their body. Once
their work with SCP-1007-RU is finished, they

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:37.200
must take a sterilizing shower to wash any
potentially lingering harmful particles from

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.980
their body, and if that’s not enough, they’re
forced into a six hour quarantine, isolated

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:48.150
from the rest of the Foundation until their
superiors are absolutely sure that they don’t

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.120
exhibit signs of infection.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:56.900
If personnel are by chance contaminated after
contact with SCP-1007-RU, the Foundation takes

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:02.760
their best interests into account and immediately
euthanizes them, followed by a cremation of

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:09.040
their remains, to make sure all biological
material is destroyed entirely, as harmful,

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.630
infectious agents may still persist on skin
tissue and inside the body long after death

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:15.640
has occured.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:22.720
Yes, the containment procedure for SCP-1007-RU
is immediate termination of a valuable Foundation

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:28.720
employee. Those don’t grow on trees either,
and the Foundation definitely does not resort

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:36.560
to this option very often, but this only demonstrates
the severe threat that SCP-1007-RU poses to

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.980
the Foundation’s integrity. Perhaps losing
one employee is better than the innumerable

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.850
deaths caused by a full scale outbreak of
the anomaly.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:52.440
The area surrounding SCP-1007-RU’s containment
chamber, located in a facility kept inside

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.480
the larger Foundation grouping of Zone-07,
is also kept free of contamination by a high-temperature

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:05.570
sterilization process as a final security
measure to keep SCP-1007-RU’s containment

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:13.330
as safe as it can possibly be. Since SCP-1007-RU
is transmitted like most contagious viral

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:18.430
diseases, via airborne, physical, and blood
contact, the Foundation has made sure their

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:23.690
containment procedures are as safe and tightly
designed as possible. Since anyone who comes

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:29.080
into contact with the anomaly is a carrier
of it, all of the precaution is understandably

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.080
necessary.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:38.970
But what is SCP-1007-RU, aside from a deadly,
infectious disease? What makes it anomalous,

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:42.450
and separates it from an ordinary virus?

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:48.360
SCP-1007-RU specifically involves the multi-step
mutation of neurons. If you don’t already

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.490
know, neurons are cells that transmit and
receive nerve impulses throughout our bodies.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:59.050
Neurons respond to stimuli, sensations like
touch, sound, light, and information from

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:04.140
other cells. They’re an essential part of
our bodies, and a necessary component for

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:10.710
cells to communicate with one another. But
most importantly, neurons help us feel pain.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:17.580
When SCP-1007-RU infects a subject, it changes
their neurons over time to allow them to feel

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.760
an increased threshold of pain tolerance,
meaning that the victim can feel a more intense

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:27.480
amount of pain before succumbing to death
or losing consciousness.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:32.960
That almost sounds beneficial, right? If everyone
had an increased pain tolerance, things like

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:39.100
minor cuts or falling off your chair would
barely register as harmful. But SCP-1007-RU

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:44.840
has a disadvantageous trade-off that comes
with its multi-step nature. As the virus mutates

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:51.330
and changes, it does so in ‘steps’, but
before each stage of cell mutation occurs,

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:57.240
the victim experiences enough pain to completely
overwhelm their pain tolerance threshold.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:02.820
SCP-1007-RU’s initial incubation period
lasts from two to four hours, after which,

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.180
the virus will make its way through the central
nervous system and into the brain. The victim

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:12.940
experiences severe pain in line with their
ordinary pain threshold, and promptly loses

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:18.150
consciousness. After they regain consciousness,
the true horrors of SCP-1007-RU commence,

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:24.810
and the anomaly begins to mutate their neurons
and alter their existing pain thresholds to

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.540
accomodate more stimuli.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:33.940
SCP-1007-RU seems to have an indefinite number
of stages. If the victim can handle the pain,

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:39.300
the infection will persist, and the neurons
will continue to mutate until they’re unable

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:44.740
to suffer any more and die from the disease.
Technically speaking, the virus is infinite,

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:49.790
and it will go on until death occurs, but
Foundation research has found that human subjects

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:55.720
have only been able to reach, at most, the
anomaly’s sixth stage, after which they

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:01.090
die. Not a single test subject has persisted
into the seventh iteration of the virus, as

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:04.639
it’s believed to be too much pain for the
human body to handle.

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:09.500
But if a subject did reach these impossible
pain thresholds, they most likely wouldn’t

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:15.901
last much longer. Curiously, when the Foundation
experimented with SCP-1007-RU on a rat, it

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:21.380
survived nine stages into the anomaly. However,
the pain was too much for the researchers

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.530
to bear observing, and the decision was made
to put the poor creature out of its misery

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.030
shortly after.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:32.200
Each stage follows a similar pattern, allowing
it to be predictably catalogued and measured

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:37.200
across all test subjects. First, a subject
will experience severe pain just below their

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.610
current pain tolerance threshold. After 36
hours, the pain will intensify, growing larger

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:47.790
and more harmful for the victim, until they
finally lose consciousness. A few minutes

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:52.330
later, when the subject has fully regained
consciousness, the next stage begins, and

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:58.670
the process repeats itself. Only this time,
the pain threshold is increased. Over time,

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:04.610
this process will continue to repeat itself
and grow more deadly, until the subject expires,

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:09.030
dying from severe levels of pain beyond any
of our comprehension.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:14.140
What makes the disease even worse to contract
is that this pain is unable to be suppressed.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:19.630
The Foundation has certainly tried, from analgesics
to tranquilizers, and surely some memetic

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:25.120
agents designed to reduce painful sensations,
but nothing has had any effect on an individual

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:32.500
infected by SCP-1007-RU. They’re forced
to endure the pain, without any reprieve,

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.650
for a full 36 hours before passing out. They
can’t even lose consciousness before the

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:45.800
stage ends, meaning that the only break from
SCP-1007-RU is the few short minutes in between

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.800
stages, all before the process repeats itself
again and again.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:55.690
Interestingly, the inactive period between
stages, labeled the “quiescence” period,

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:01.760
seems to increase exponentially as time goes
on. The first period ranges from 48 to 108

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:06.550
hours, where the subject feels completely
ordinary before the next active stage occurs

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:09.020
and their pain tolerance is increased.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:13.240
The Foundation typically does not like to
prolong the pain of its test subjects beyond

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:18.700
what’s absolutely necessary to understand
all elements of an anomaly. The moral issues

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:24.540
that resulted from SCP-1007-RU’s research
were addressed in a statement by Overseer

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:30.070
O5-4, which read “Human experiments are
performed only with the explicit permission

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:34.020
of the Overseer Council. Any requests for
experiments in which a subject would have

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:39.550
to reach the sixth stage are rejected automatically.
First, try to imagine such pain.”

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:46.170
But regardless, experiments involving SCP-1007-RU
have been performed for the purposes of gaining

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.040
all of this information, and the Foundation
kept recorded transcripts of some of them.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:55.830
One interview, which was held 2 hours, 12
minutes after the first exposure to the virus,

00:10:55.830 --> 00:11:01.010
and then held again at 2 hours and 17 minutes
following infection, involved an interaction

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.120
between Dr. Luginin and an unfortunate patient.

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:08.779
First, the patient felt fine, and asked if
the researcher had infected them with something.

00:11:08.779 --> 00:11:13.330
When asked to describe how they felt, they
exclaimed that they felt fine, and had been

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:18.970
sitting there for two hours feeling normal.
Then, the virus took root, and a howling scream

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:24.690
filled the room. The patient began to sob
and scream, feeling pain unlike anything else

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:29.640
they had felt before. Pain they didn’t know
they were capable of feeling. They called

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:34.920
for Dr. Luginin to stop the experiment, asking
why this was happening to them, but Luginin’s

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:39.740
assistant called for the subject to be restrained
and locked up. As the pain increased, they

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:43.690
became desperate, confessing to the crimes
that they had committed prior to being imprisoned

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:49.420
and drafted as a Foundation D-Class personnel,
and begging the Foundation to stop. But even

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:54.300
if the Foundation wanted to, they couldn’t.
There was nothing they could do but watch.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:59.180
Adhering to procedure, Dr. Luginin calmly
told the subject to relax themselves and asked

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:04.339
where they were feeling the pain. But the
subject continued to scream, barely able to

00:12:04.339 --> 00:12:10.610
get the words out. Their head, skin, heart,
stomach, bones and teeth, every last bit of

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:16.240
their body was overwhelmed with nothing but
pure pain. The subject begged and pleaded,

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:22.371
and struggled for hours until they eventually
lost consciousness. Upon coming to, the subject

00:12:22.371 --> 00:12:28.080
asked what happened, to which Dr. Luginin’s
assistant, Junior Researcher Kosmov, responded

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.510
that he’ll certainly remember in two days.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:35.560
Dr. Luginin was rightfully mortified by what
he witnessed on that day, and protested further

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:42.100
experimentation with SCP-1007-RU. Luginin
appeared before the Overseer council, and

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:47.100
advocated for the destruction of the virus,
but the O5’s were unable to accomodate his

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:52.310
request, as they had already severely limited
the experiments and were unsure of how to

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:58.801
take measures to eradicate the virus completely.
Luginin withdrew from the SCP-1007-RU research

00:12:58.801 --> 00:13:04.430
project, and the position of research head
was given to his assistant, Junior Researcher

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:10.520
Kosmov. Despite Kosmov’s inexperience and
sadistic tendencies to prolong and observe

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:15.710
experiences, Luginin was let go. However,
Kosmov’s psychological evaluation was still

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:20.910
within the lines of what the Foundation considered
acceptable, and he was given permission to

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:26.920
have complete control over all SCP-1007-RU
research materials.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:32.330
The file ends with a single note, written
by Kosmov shortly after his promotion to Research

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:33.330
Head:

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:38.250
“Permission has been granted for experiments
involving humans up to stage nine - M. S.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.460
Kosmov”

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:45.459
Now go check out “SCP-610 - The Flesh That
Hates” and “SCP-500 - Panacea” for more

00:13:45.459 --> 00:13:47.929
anomalous diseases and cures!

